  "limitations": [
    "The recovery-entry detector executes in an emulator over authored state with the boot-reason reader, power check, key poll and delay supplied; the key poll writes a scripted per-index button sequence and the power check writes its flag into the quiet stack window. No real key matrix, power rail or timer is read.",
    "The boot manager 0x80c00454 and the final main boot 0x80c00918 are not re-executed here; their control flow is read statically. The upgrade-record software recovery request and the recovery image validation are covered elsewhere.",
    "This establishes the recovery-entry conditions, not the physical key mapping, the real debounce timing, the power threshold or that recovery can always restore a good image after a bad write. With no USB/wired port (BLE bridge only), these two-key-plus-power and upgrade-record paths are the only recovery entries, and both still need on-device confirmation."
  ],
